  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "When a certain metal surface is illuminated with light of frequency $v$, the stopping potential for photoelectric current is $V_{0}$. When the same surface is illuminated by light of frequency $\\frac{v}{2}$ the stopping potential is $\\frac{V_{0}}{4} .$ The threshold\r\nfrequency for photoelectric, emission is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "YCYTl",
      "text": "$\\frac{v}{6}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "3lv8b",
      "text": "$\\frac{v}{3}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "lxvOs",
      "text": "$\\frac{2 v}{3}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "R9y9I",
      "text": "$\\frac{4 v}{3}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Ist case\r\n$$\r\n\\begin{array}{l}\r\nh v=h v_{0}+e V_{0} \\\\\r\n\\frac{h v}{2}=h v_{0}+\\frac{e V_{0}}{4}\r\n\\end{array}\r\n$$\r\nSolving Eqs. (i) and (ii), we get\r\n$$\r\nv_{0}=\\frac{v}{3}\r\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
